<title>UK: PowerGen makes five pct share buyback.</title>
<headline>PowerGen makes five pct share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British electricity generator PowerGen Plc said on Thursday it had instructed UBS Limited and Kleinwort Benson Securities Limited as agents to buy up to five percent of its capital or 33.5 million shares.</p>
<p>PowerGen said at its half year results on November 14 that it intended to buy back up to 10 percent of its shares &quot;when appropriate.&quot;  </p>
<p>PowerGen shares were trading at 574.5 pence, up three pence, by 0915 GMT after opening at 570 pence.</p>
<p>At those levels, the five percent buyback would cost PowerGen some 167.5 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
